# === GAP PROBES -- CAN EACH REFUTATION ACTUALLY SUCCEED? ===================
# ADDED 2026-09-09. NO NUMBER IN THIS FILE MOVED, AND THAT IS THE FINDING.
#
# scripts/ci/check_mutation_coverage.py counts STAGES: `must-fail-cases-total`
# and `stages-with-check` are derived from `check_proof:` blocks, and an
# `unsupported:` entry has none. So on 2026-09-09 eight gap fixtures were added,
# `signoff.py prove` went from 181 cases over 1 gap probe to 189 over 9, and
# this ledger's four asserted numbers did not change by one:
#
#   blocking-unproven          0  ->  0
#   report-unproven            4  ->  4
#   must-fail-cases-total    142  -> 142
#   stages-with-check         28  ->  28
#
# The checker was RUN and prints "ci/MUTATION_COVERAGE agrees with
# ci/signoff.yaml". It is right, and it is blind here, in exactly the way this
# file's own header warns about the green line: "`prove` skips these stages
# entirely -- they do not appear in its case count, so the green N problem(s): 0
# line says nothing whatever about them." Substitute "gap probes" for "stages"
# and the sentence still holds. The rows below are therefore NOT asserted by any
# checker -- they are a hand-kept record, and they are marked as such rather
# than dressed up as a measurement.
#
# WHY GAP PROBES BELONG IN A GATE-COVERAGE LEDGER AT ALL. A `refuted_by:` that
# exits 1 is what keeps a permanent exemption alive. Nine of them decide which
# rows stay NOT-MEASURED forever in a graded evidence report. Before this date
# EIGHT of the nine had never been shown capable of exiting 0 -- `prove` printed
# "executed by lint but has never been shown to discriminate" and counted it as
# no problem. An attempted refutation that cannot succeed is a gate that cannot
# fail with the sign flipped, and this ledger exists for exactly that shape.
#
# HAND-KEPT, NOT ASSERTED. Fixtures live at ci/fixtures/gap-<id>/{still-real,
# refuted}/ and are found by convention; nothing in the manifest declares them,
# so nothing goes red if one is deleted except `prove` quietly returning to
# "NO FIXTURE". Provenance, decoys and known limits: ci/fixtures/README.md.
#
#   gap                             cases   fixture pair
#   d2d-tx-clock-boundary-untimed     2     constraints.sdc with / without the
#                                           `-group [get_clocks $_tx_grp]` cut
#   sta-hold-coverage                 2     pre-existing; the hold coverage
#                                           report present / absent
#   antenna-signoff                   2     a manifest with / without a stage
#                                           whose id names antennas
#   metal-density-fill                2     4b_pnr_route_eval.tcl with
#                                           EVR_METAL_FILL defaulting 0 / 1
#   gds-completeness                  2     a PDK stand-in with / without a
#                                           *_BE package directory
#   lvs                               2     a PDK stand-in with / without
#                                           transistor-level CDL over 1 kB
#   dynamic-ir-drop                   2     a PDK stand-in with / without cell
#                                           SPICE over 1 kB
#   io-rail-ir-drop                   2     a generated CPF declaring / not
#                                           declaring VDDIO at column 1
#   full-design-lint-gating           2     a manifest whose stages do / do not
#                                           run verif/lint/full/run.sh
#
# 18 cases, 9 probes, all green under `signoff.py prove` on 2026-09-09.
#
# WHAT WAS ACTUALLY CHECKED, because a count is not a review:
#   * every `refuted_by:` was read against the CLAIM its `reason:` makes, and
#     the refuting artefact identified as a thing that could arrive -- not as a
#     rewording. Four of the nine turn on vendor collateral this site does not
#     have; for those the fixture stages the collateral APPEARING, in synthetic
#     form, and never in real form (public repository, and these gaps are ABOUT
#     vendor collateral).
#   * both halves were run: still-real must exit 1, refuted must exit 0. A pair
